{title: Come Ye Sinners Poor and Needy}
{key: Am}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Am]Come ye [F]sinners [C]poor and [G]needy [Em]weak and [F]wounded [Am]sick and [C]sore
[C]Jesus [Am]ready [G]stands to [Am]save you [**]full of [F]pity [Em]love and [Am]pow'r
[Am]I will [F]arise and [C]go to [G]Jesus, [Em]He will em[F]brace me [Am]in His [C]arms
[C]In the [Am]arms of [G]my dear [Am]Savior, [F]oh, there [G]are ten [Em]thousand [Am]charms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Am]Come, ye [F]thirsty, [C]come, and [G]welcome, [Em]God's free [F]bounty [Am]glori[C]fy
[C]True be[Am]lief and [G]true re[Am]pentance, [**]every [F]grace that [Em]brings you [Am]nigh
[Am]I will [F]arise and [C]go to [G]Jesus, [Em]He will em[F]brace me [Am]in His [C]arms
[C]In the [Am]arms of [G]my dear [Am]Savior, [F]oh, there [G]are ten [Em]thousand [Am]charms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Am]View Him [F]prostrate [C]in the [G]garden; [Em]on the [F]ground your [Am]Maker [C]lies
[C]On the [Am]bloody [G]tree be[Am]hold Him; [**]sinner, [F]will this [Em]not suf[Am]fice?
[Am]I will [F]arise and [C]go to [G]Jesus, [Em]He will em[F]brace me [Am]in His [C]arms
[C]In the [Am]arms of [G]my dear [Am]Savior, [F]oh, there [G]are ten [Em]thousand [Am]charms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Am]Let not [F]conscience [C]make you [G]linger' [Em]Nor of [F]fitness [Am]fondly [C]dream
[C]All the [Am]fitness [G]He re[Am]quireth; [**]is to [F]feel your [Em]need of [Am]Him
[Am]I will [F]arise and [C]go to [G]Jesus, [Em]He will em[F]brace me [Am]in His [C]arms
[C]In the [Am]arms of [G]my dear [Am]Savior, [F]oh, there [G]are ten [Em]thousand [Am]charms.
{end_of_verse}
